cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BioSwarm: bio-inspired coordination for teams of AI agents, and the open research behind it"
message: "If you use this research or software, please cite it as below, and name the study and the commit you used."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Unfold Research"
    website: "https://unfold.host"
repository-code: "https://github.com/unfold-research/bioswarm"
url: "https://unfold.host/research/"
abstract: >-
  BioSwarm is the coordination engine of Colony and the open record of Unfold Research: preregistered studies of
  whether mechanisms from natural collectives (stigmergy, lateral inhibition, requirement traces and others) coordinate
  teams of AI agents better than a manager agent or a group chat, with hypotheses, reports, independent reviews and
  failures. No advantage over a single agent or a manager agent is claimed.
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - AI agents
  - swarm intelligence
  - stigmergy
  - bio-inspired coordination
  - open research
  - preregistration
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-11-27"
